    "result_text": "The build passes. \n\nI extended the business-day rule to public holidays by updating the single shared `BusinessDay.rollForward` utility (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/BusinessDay.java`), which both `Owner.defaultRegistrationDate()` and `ClinicServiceImpl.resolveRegistrationDate()` already delegate to \u2014 so no logic was duplicated.\n\nChanges:\n- Added the fixed holiday list (2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28) as a constant.\n- Replaced the weekend-only shift with a loop that rolls forward one day at a time until it lands on a `isBusinessDay` \u2014 a small private helper that treats Saturdays, Sundays, and listed holidays as non-business days. This correctly handles chains (e.g. 2026-12-25 Fri \u2192 26/27 weekend \u2192 28 holiday \u2192 29 Tue).\n\nThe test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing including the acceptance check that the default registration date never falls on a weekend).",
